<Folder><name>Golf courses (10)</name>
<Placemark><name>Poppy Hills GC, hole 9 tee</name><styleUrl>#tK</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Known patch</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>Your known patch. Hole 9 starts in the far south-east corner of the course, and the star sits on its tee. Wood chips filled all the non-planted ground when the course reopened in 2014, as irrigated turf fell from 82 to 62 acres. A 2021-22 project then built five new tees (holes 4, 5, 8, 12, 17) and enlarged five more (6, 10, 14, 15, 16).<br><br>Access: Private course in play. Ask the pro shop before walking it.<br><br><a href="https://www.amateurgolf.com/11890-GolfNews-Poppy-Hills-Redesign-A-Pebble-Beach-California-Course-Review">Opening-day review, Mar 2014</a><br><br><a href="https://blog.ncga.org/poppy-hills-changing-looks">2021-22 refinements</a><br><br>36.57784, -121.93547]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.935470,36.577840,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pebble Beach Golf Links, first tee and pro shop</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>Red spy in June 2023, 40 m from the first tee and beside the pro shop. A June fruiting points to an irrigated chip bed. No chip installation is documented for the course itself.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 90 m (Jun 2023): red spy ×1.<br><br>Access: Resort grounds open to visitors.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/169542938">Record, Jun 25 2023</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/169542938">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.56905, -121.94968]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.949680,36.569050,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Poppy Hills hole 12, north end</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>Gymnopilus aurantiophyllus and G. ventricosus beside the 12th fairway on Dec 29, 2023. These are the only chip-fungus records on the course.<br><br>Access: Private course in play. Ask the pro shop before walking it.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/195322049">Record, Dec 29 2023</a><br><br>36.58987, -121.93748]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.937480,36.589870,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Poppy Hills hole 15 tee, rebuilt 2021-22</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>The Jones tee here was expanded and reconfigured in 2021-22, and the hole 14 green beside it was reshaped in the same project. Whether the surround was re-chipped is not documented.<br><br>Access: Private course in play. Ask the pro shop before walking it.<br><br><a href="https://blog.ncga.org/poppy-hills-changing-looks">2021-22 refinements</a><br><br>36.58578, -121.93994]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.939940,36.585780,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Poppy Hills hole 12, new back tee 2021-22</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>New tee built in the 2021-22 refinements project, the most recent construction on the course. The pin marks the mapped tee, and the new deck sits behind it. Chips around it are not documented.<br><br>Access: Private course in play. Ask the pro shop before walking it.<br><br><a href="https://blog.ncga.org/poppy-hills-changing-looks">2021-22 refinements</a><br><br>36.58800, -121.93837]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.938370,36.588000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Poppy Hills hole 17, new back tee 2021-22</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>New tee built in the 2021-22 refinements project, the most recent construction on the course. The pin marks the mapped tee, and the new deck sits behind it. Chips around it are not documented.<br><br>Access: Private course in play. Ask the pro shop before walking it.<br><br><a href="https://blog.ncga.org/poppy-hills-changing-looks">2021-22 refinements</a><br><br>36.58389, -121.94107]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.941070,36.583890,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Poppy Hills hole 4, new back tee 2021-22</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>New tee built in the 2021-22 refinements project, the most recent construction on the course. The pin marks the mapped tee, and the new deck sits behind it. Chips around it are not documented.<br><br>Access: Private course in play. Ask the pro shop before walking it.<br><br><a href="https://blog.ncga.org/poppy-hills-changing-looks">2021-22 refinements</a><br><br>36.58078, -121.94443]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.944430,36.580780,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Poppy Hills hole 5, new back tee 2021-22</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>New tee built in the 2021-22 refinements project, the most recent construction on the course. The pin marks the mapped tee, and the new deck sits behind it. Chips around it are not documented.<br><br>Access: Private course in play. Ask the pro shop before walking it.<br><br><a href="https://blog.ncga.org/poppy-hills-changing-looks">2021-22 refinements</a><br><br>36.57942, -121.93825]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.938250,36.579420,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Poppy Hills hole 8, new back tee 2021-22</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>New tee built in the 2021-22 refinements project, the most recent construction on the course. The pin marks the mapped tee, and the new deck sits behind it. Chips around it are not documented.<br><br>Access: Private course in play. Ask the pro shop before walking it.<br><br><a href="https://blog.ncga.org/poppy-hills-changing-looks">2021-22 refinements</a><br><br>36.58058, -121.93919]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.939190,36.580580,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Links at Spanish Bay, rebuild in progress</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>Closed on Mar 18, 2026 for a full rebuild and due to reopen in spring 2027. Its new landscaping will be the freshest mulch in the forest, too new to fruit this season. Mulch maid on the east edge in Feb 2023.<br><br>Access: Construction site until 2027.<br><br><a href="https://blog.ncga.org/pebble-beach-co.-announces-timeline-for-gil-hanse-spanish-bay-renovation">Rebuild timeline</a><br><br>36.61160, -121.94280]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.942800,36.611600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Known patches (2)</name>
<Placemark><name>Bank of America planter, 200 E Franklin St</name><styleUrl>#tK</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Known patch</b> · Monterey<br><br>Your report of P. cyanescens in this planter. Street View from Sep 2024 shows a raised brick planter under a clipped hedge on the north-facing wall.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 160 m (Jan 2023): mulch maid ×1.<br><br>Access: Bank frontage. Sidewalk side only.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/146566990">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.59947, -121.89317]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.893170,36.599470,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Huckleberry Hill trailhead, 4011 Los Altos Dr</name><styleUrl>#tK</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Known patch</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>Your report of P. cyanescens at this trailhead. Six Gymnopilus aurantiophyllus and two red spy records run from here to about 1 km north-north-west, Dec 21 to 30, 2022. A Shroomery poster picked about 40 P. cyanescens in a month from one forest spot on the Peninsula in March 2020, location not given.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 300 m (Dec 2022): red spy ×1.<br><br>Access: Inside the Pebble Beach gates.<br><br><a href="https://www.shroomery.org/forums/showflat.php/Number/26567391">Forest-patch post, Mar 2020</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/144993793">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.58771, -121.92321]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.923210,36.587710,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Psilocybe recorded (6)</name>
<Placemark><name>CSUMB library beds</name><styleUrl>#tP</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded</b> · Seaside<br><br>P. allenii photographed beside the library on Nov 16, 2025 (±9 m). A second record the same day sits about 300 m west (±830 m).<br><br>3 wood-chip fungus records within 170 m (Feb 2024): landscaping morel ×3.<br><br>Access: Open university grounds. Look along bed edges beside the paths.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/326920753">Record, Nov 16 2025</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/326925723">Second record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/200124086">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/200127006">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.65273, -121.79587]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.795865,36.652733,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>CSUMB, 8th Ave side</name><styleUrl>#tP</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded</b> · Seaside / Marina<br><br>P. allenii on Dec 2, 2025 (±18 m).<br><br>2 wood-chip fungus records within 230 m (Nov 2021): red spy ×2.<br><br>Access: Open university grounds.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/329508313">Record, Dec 2 2025</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/102569249">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/100715269">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.65530, -121.80228]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.802283,36.655300,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pine Ave, 200 block</name><styleUrl>#tP</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded</b> · Pacific Grove<br><br>P. allenii on Nov 11, 2025 (±9 m). Red spy turned up in planters about 450 m east the same month.<br><br>Access: The point is a private frontage. Check public parkway strips only.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/326098232">Record, Nov 11 2025</a><br><br>36.61642, -121.91013]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.910134,36.616424,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Carmel-by-the-Sea (approximate)</name><styleUrl>#tA</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded, location approximate</b> · Carmel<br><br>P. allenii fruited at the front door of a holiday rental on Jan 2, 2022, per a Shroomery post. No address is given, so the pin marks the village centre.<br><br>Access: Private frontages. Public planting strips only.<br><br><a href="https://www.shroomery.org/forums/showflat.php/Number/27604142">Shroomery post, Jan 2 2022</a><br><br>36.55520, -121.92330]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.923300,36.555200,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>King City, Broadway St (inferred town)</name><styleUrl>#tA</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded, location approximate</b> · King City<br><br>P. allenii filled a restaurant garden on a main street on Nov 22, 2019, in a south-county town 40 minutes from Paso Robles. King City is an inference from that drive time. The bed was shaded by the building, under roses, with wet soil.<br><br>Access: Business frontage. Sidewalk side only.<br><br><a href="https://www.shroomery.org/forums/showflat.php/Number/26337778">Shroomery thread, Nov 2019</a><br><br>36.21280, -121.12620]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.126200,36.212800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Monterey (approximate)</name><styleUrl>#tA</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded, location approximate</b> · Monterey<br><br>P. allenii on Jan 11, 2006, recorded only as Monterey. The location is only good to about 3.4 km.<br><br><a href="https://mycoportal.org/portal/collections/individual/index.php?occid=7973974">Record, Jan 11 2006</a><br><br>36.59650, -121.86900]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.869000,36.596500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Candidate sites (18)</name>
<Placemark><name>CSUMB Arts and Humanities, south side</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Seaside<br><br>Lattice stinkhorn (May 2026) and stubble rosegill about 17 m off the south wall.<br><br>Access: Open university grounds.<br><br>36.65204, -121.79833]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.798330,36.652040,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>CSUMB Chapman Science, west wall</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Seaside<br><br>Landscaping morels and Gymnopilus aurantiophyllus about 15 m off the west wall, Feb 2024.<br><br>3 wood-chip fungus records within 60 m (Feb 2024): landscaping morel ×3.<br><br>Access: Open university grounds.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/200124086">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/200127006">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.65355, -121.79510]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.795100,36.653550,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>CSUMB Dining Commons, north side</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Seaside<br><br>Landscaping morel on the north side (Feb 2024) and at Otter Express next door (Feb 2019).<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 70 m (Feb 2024): landscaping morel ×1.<br><br>Access: Open university grounds.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/200574466">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.65491, -121.79914]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.799140,36.654910,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>CSUMB Green Hall</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Seaside<br><br>Bird's nest fungi and blewits at the north-east corner, 2010 to Mar 2025.<br><br>Access: Open university grounds.<br><br>36.65213, -121.79052]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.790520,36.652130,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>CSUMB north campus</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Marina<br><br>Imjin Rd side of campus and the UC MBEST center.<br><br>4 wood-chip fungus records within 260 m (Apr 2017 to Apr 2024): landscaping morel ×2, mulch maid ×2.<br><br>Access: Open university grounds.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/205130032">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/47370142">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.65687, -121.79385]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.793850,36.656870,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>CSUMB south campus</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Seaside<br><br>Joe Lloyd Way and Divarty St beds. Newest record is Feb 2026.<br><br>4 wood-chip fungus records within 300 m (Feb 2021 to Feb 2026): mulch maid ×2, landscaping morel ×1, red spy ×1.<br><br>Access: Open university grounds.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/199229007">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/69580536">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.64860, -121.79560]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.795600,36.648600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Canyon Del Rey chip strip, Laguna Grande</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Seaside<br><br>Street View from Aug 2024 shows coarse wood chips under a row of purple-leaf plums, in the strip between Canyon Del Rey Blvd and the park lot from about 1167 to 1191 Canyon Del Rey.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 200 m (Mar 2025): mulch maid ×1.<br><br>Access: City park frontage. Park in the lot off Canyon Del Rey.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/265622666">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.60266, -121.85391]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.853910,36.602660,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casa del Oro garden</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Monterey<br><br>Logged as growing in a mulched bed in the State Historic Park gardens by Custom House Plaza.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 150 m (Dec 2024): red spy ×1.<br><br>Access: State historic park grounds. Look, don't collect.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/256531501">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.60280, -121.89477]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.894770,36.602800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Del Monte Ave eucalyptus chips, Navy School gate</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Monterey<br><br>An iNaturalist note from Jun 2025 describes chips 3 to 4 inches deep, likely eucalyptus, spread here months to a year earlier. Lattice stinkhorns fruited in Jun 2025 and Jun 2026. Untested for Psilocybe.<br><br>Access: Monterey Bay Coastal Trail.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/293967713">Chip note, Jun 2025</a><br><br>36.60009, -121.87549]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.875490,36.600090,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Eardley Ave lot at Central Ave</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Pacific Grove<br><br>Red spy in Nov 2025 and five yellow fieldcap records in Jan and Feb 2024, about 450 m east of the Pine Ave record.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 130 m (Nov 2025): red spy ×1.<br><br>Access: Parking-lot edges.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/327707140">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.61738, -121.90477]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.904770,36.617380,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Elkhorn Slough Reserve visitor center</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Elkhorn<br><br>A wood-chip specialist logged by the visitor center in Feb 2023.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 300 m (Feb 2023): A. putaminum ×1.<br><br>Access: Research reserve. Look, don't collect.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/151691976">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.81715, -121.72920]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.729200,36.817150,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>George Washington Park</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Pacific Grove<br><br>OpenStreetMap maps five of this park's paths as wood mulch, which fits the fungus records.<br><br>7 wood-chip fungus records within 330 m (Feb 1998 to Jan 2024): mulch maid ×4, red spy ×2, A. praecox ×1.<br><br>Access: City park.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/197343232">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/37856104">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.61984, -121.92866]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.928660,36.619840,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Haul Road trail</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Del Monte Forest<br><br>Red spy along the Haul Road trail in Dec 2019 and Dec 2022, just east of the Poppy Hills fairways.<br><br>2 wood-chip fungus records within 560 m (Dec 2019 to Dec 2022): red spy ×2.<br><br>Access: Del Monte Forest trail inside the Pebble Beach gates.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/144993793">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/36990586">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.58810, -121.92600]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.926000,36.588100,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mission Trail Preserve</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Carmel<br><br>Flanders Trail beside the Rowntree native plant garden.<br><br>2 wood-chip fungus records within 250 m (Jan 2019 to Mar 2019): red spy ×2.<br><br>Access: City nature preserve.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/21583625">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/19467603">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.54896, -121.91625]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.916250,36.548960,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Oldemeyer Center, Wheeler St side</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Seaside<br><br>Street View from Aug 2024 shows wood-chip beds with ornamental grasses along the building frontage on Wheeler St.<br><br>Access: City community center at 986 Hilby Ave. Park on Wheeler St.<br><br>36.60213, -121.84537]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.845370,36.602130,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Quarry Park</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Monterey<br><br>Red spy three times across two winters beside Via Ladera.<br><br>3 wood-chip fungus records within 260 m (Dec 2022 to Dec 2023): red spy ×3.<br><br>Access: City park.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/148434818">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/194840654">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.59343, -121.90904]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.909040,36.593430,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Rip Van Winkle Open Space</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Pacific Grove<br><br>Records cluster at the Country Club Gate and Forest Lodge Rd edges of the open space.<br><br>6 wood-chip fungus records within 420 m (Jan 2023 to Jan 2024): red spy ×4, mulch maid ×2.<br><br>Access: City open space, open 7 am to 8 pm.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/197642355">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/197998948">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.60850, -121.92950]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.929500,36.608500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ryan Ranch office park</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Monterey<br><br>Parking-lot bed on Upper Ragsdale Dr. Irrigated office-park beds are the classic Bay Area wavy-cap habitat.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 250 m (Feb 2024): red spy ×1.<br><br>Access: Private office park. Stay on public frontage.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/199483210">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.57929, -121.81578]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.815780,36.579290,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Thin-evidence candidates (6)</name>
<Placemark><name>Del Monte Forest Green Loop trail</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Pebble Beach<br><br>Gymnopilus aurantiophyllus in Dec 2024 and Mar 2025.<br><br>Access: Forest trail.<br><br>36.59571, -121.93527]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.935270,36.595710,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Doud St and Colton St</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Monterey<br><br>Red spy (Dec 2020) and landscaping morels (Aug 2022).<br><br>3 wood-chip fungus records within 120 m (Dec 2020 to Aug 2022): landscaping morel ×2, red spy ×1.<br><br>Access: Residential. Public strips only.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/130536844">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/130540940">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.59207, -121.89912]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.899120,36.592070,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Imjin Pkwy at Logan Way</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Marina<br><br>A single landscaping morel in Jan 2026, which points to fresh mulch in the new plantings here.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 200 m (Jan 2026): landscaping morel ×1.<br><br>Access: Public roadside plantings.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/337361352">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.66205, -121.79154]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.791540,36.662050,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ocean Ave planters</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Carmel<br><br>Downtown planters along Ocean Ave.<br><br>2 wood-chip fungus records within 260 m (Mar 2021 to Jan 2024): red spy ×1, A. praecox ×1.<br><br>Access: Public sidewalk strips.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/196253798">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/72048639">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.55505, -121.92620]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.926200,36.555050,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Palo Corona park, Rancho Cañada trails</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Carmel<br><br>Three stubble rosegill and one yellow fieldcap record from four observers, Jan 2025 to Jan 2026. Both species also grow in grass, so chips are unconfirmed. No Street View here.<br><br>Access: Regional park trails. Check the park district's rules before collecting.<br><br>36.53951, -121.89031]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.890310,36.539510,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Veterans Memorial Park, east side</name><styleUrl>#tW</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site, thin evidence</b> · Monterey<br><br>Gymnopilus aurantiophyllus, mulch maid and yellow fieldcap here, Dec 2022 to Feb 2025. Street View from Aug 2024 shows pine duff and no chips at the trailhead lot 250 m west.<br><br>1 wood-chip fungus record within 160 m (Feb 2025): mulch maid ×1.<br><br>Access: City park.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/261804136">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.59984, -121.91072]]></description><Point><coordinates>-121.910720,36.599840,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Santa Cruz side (27)</name>
<Placemark><name>Delaware Ave at Fair Ave</name><styleUrl>#tP</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded</b> · Santa Cruz<br><br>Three P. allenii observations on Dec 3, 2024.<br><br>Access: The point is a private frontage. Check public parkway strips only.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/254050439">Record 1</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/254050265">Record 2</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/254051125">Record 3</a><br><br>36.95604, -122.04510]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.045095,36.956042,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>River St at Harvey West</name><styleUrl>#tP</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded</b> · Santa Cruz<br><br>P. allenii on Nov 24, 2022, logged as garden mulch after rain and lows in the upper 30s.<br><br>2 wood-chip fungus records within 200 m (Dec 2020 to Jan 2021): red spy ×2.<br><br>Access: Business district. Stick to public frontage.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/142770465">Record, Nov 24 2022</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/68832118">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/67209548">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.99111, -122.03229]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.032294,36.991111,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>UCSC Coastal Science Campus</name><styleUrl>#tP</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded</b> · Santa Cruz<br><br>P. allenii on Dec 2, 2018 (±200 m), inside the densest wood-chip fungus cluster on the bay. OpenStreetMap maps a wood-chip path here.<br><br>51 wood-chip fungus records within 420 m (Dec 2016 to Jan 2026): mulch maid ×18, red spy ×17, A. praecox ×14, A. putaminum ×2.<br><br>Deadly galerina recorded within 420 m (Jan 2020).<br><br>Access: University grounds next to Younger Lagoon Reserve. Stay out of the reserve.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/18795415">Record, Dec 2 2018</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/336919819">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://mycoportal.org/portal/collections/individual/index.php?occid=14727843">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.95158, -122.06509]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.065094,36.951583,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>UCSC Science Hill</name><styleUrl>#tP</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded</b> · Santa Cruz<br><br>The only precisely mapped P. cyanescens on the bay: found in campus wood-chip landscaping on Jan 14, 2018. An older campus record dates to Nov 2006.<br><br>25 wood-chip fungus records within 420 m (Jan 2016 to Jan 2026): red spy ×22, A. praecox ×3.<br><br>Deadly galerina recorded within 420 m (Nov 2023).<br><br>Access: University grounds.<br><br><a href="https://mycoportal.org/portal/collections/individual/index.php?occid=8150389">Record, Jan 14 2018</a><br><br><a href="https://mycoportal.org/portal/collections/individual/index.php?occid=7975627">Record, Nov 2006</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/333870423">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/334027933">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.99960, -122.06150]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.061500,36.999600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mission Springs (approximate)</name><styleUrl>#tA</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Psilocybe recorded, location approximate</b> · Scotts Valley<br><br>P. cyanescens collected for the Dec 14, 2012 NAMA foray. The location is only good to about 2 km, so read it as somewhere around Scotts Valley.<br><br><a href="https://mycoportal.org/portal/collections/individual/index.php?occid=8076348">Record, Dec 14 2012</a><br><br>37.06250, -122.02950]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.029500,37.062500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Almar Ave lot</name><styleUrl>#tC</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Candidate site</b> · Santa Cruz<br><br>Shopping-center lot plantings.<br><br>3 wood-chip fungus records within 200 m (Nov 2017 to Feb 2024): red spy ×2, A. praecox ×1.<br><br>Access: Private lot. Stay on public frontage.<br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/99978400">Indicator record</a><br><br><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/8900820">Indicator record</a><br><br>36.96160, -122.04450]]></description><Point><coordinates>-122.044500,36.961600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
